[~accountid:712020:d4fea1a1-04d3-411a-82fc-435abbd538e3], thanks for sharing the below. In short, we are in need to follow the baliff’s request. Thus the following steps on our side should be as follows:

a) send a proper email notice to the bailiff acknowledging the receipt of the order and confirming that we will comply and will make the payments due to the debtor (if any) to the bank account indicated by the bailiff. Also, we ask the bailiff to update us on when we can change the bank account back to the driver's bank account;

b) inform the driver that his account is seized and as of XX date the payouts (if any) will be made in favour of the third party (*don't* disclose this third party) based on the bailiff's order No XXX (to manage the driver's expectations, a driver should also be informed in case only a certain amount is deducted from its payouts);

c) change the bank account as per the bailiff’s request;

d) after a while once the bailiff's approval is received, change the bank account back and notify the driver accordingly.

If the accounting team has any uncertainties with regard to deductions, please feel free to ask the bailiff those questions by way of responding to the received order.

Hope this helps, but please let me know if you have nay further questions. Thanks!

